{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-spectral-decomposition-qvalue-table1-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:spectral-decomposition-qvalue-table1-data","kind":"table","title":"Table 1 from cor:spectral-decomposition-qvalue","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/cor-spectral-decomposition-qvalue"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"spectral-decomposition-qvalue-table1-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:spectral-decomposition-qvalue-table1-data\"></a><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"center\">Knot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau(r,s)</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\">Degree</th>\n<th align=\"center\">Shell</th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}_M(\\tau \\!\\cdot\\! T_\\beta)</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\">Pauli</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau(2,3) = e</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0.52693</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau(2,5)</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">5</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0.62156</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau(2,7) = c</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">7</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0.74336</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau(3,5)</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">5</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1.94018</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau(2,9) = \\tau(2,3^2)</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">9</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">5</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0.89764</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau(3,4) = t = \\tau(3,2^2)</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">6</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0.91725</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Traces are the convention-D Markov trace (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = q^3/(q^2+1)</code>) at the proton pin <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code>, with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_\\beta = \\sigma_0\\sigma_1^{-1}</code>; the Pauli column is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">|\\mathrm{tr}_M(e_{(1^3)}\\,\\tau\\,T_\\beta\\,e_{(1^3)})|/|\\mathrm{tr}_M(T_\\beta)|</code>, which vanishes because the Ocneanu weight of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(1^3)</code> is zero under convention D. Until 2026-10-10 the trace column read <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0.3649, 0.4251, 0.5040, 1.5586, 0.6048, 0.5850</code> and the Pauli column <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0.4667, 0.3788, 0.3075, 0.2248, 0.2495, 0.2770</code>, excised convention-C values.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue-table1-data.md","heading":"Table"}
